     Sending and receiving messages through the iippmmii driver requires the use
     of ioctl(2).  The ioctls are used due to the complexity of data sent to
     and from the device.  The ioctl(2) command codes below are defined in
     <_s_y_s_/_i_p_m_i_._h>.  The third argument to ioctl(2) should be a pointer to the
     type indicated.

